      "writtenOn": "2021-02-24T18:23:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think PS3 is basically an unpolished version of the former. But it doesn\u0027t really stand on its own.\n\nI would be very surprised if there is a significant performance change base \u003c-\u003e PS3, especially given the difficulty of measuring performance changes here. The only thing that changed is argument parsing, and that\u0027s pretty trivial. We no longer need the Java argument arrays, since they\u0027re replaced by the ZygoteCommandBuffer native data structure. But we still allocate the argument strings as Java Strings, so I think Java allocation hasn\u0027t changed much. And all the allocation and overhead due to stopping threads and restarting threads is unchanged.\n\nPS2 \u003c-\u003e PS3 moves the specialization code to follow the usap model of doing the specialization in childMain, but it should do the same work as before. And it uses a code path I deleted from the final CL (and thus wasn\u0027t reviewed), making comparisons a bit unconvincing.\n\nI\u0027d indeed prefer to just submit the current version.",
      "parentUuid": "b3a0d008_642ff9fa",
      "revId": "69d44b0bfd5d4a6721ab3dccf537a147af7b6d1d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
